  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nIn one operation, you may choose a prefix of the array of length kkk (1≤k≤N1 ≤ k ≤ N1≤k≤N) and an integer X≥0X ≥ 0X≥0, and apply the bitwiseXORbitwise XORbitwiseXOR operation to all elements in that prefix:\n\n\n[Ai=Ai⊕X&nbsp;for&nbsp;all&nbsp;1≤i≤k][ A_i = A_i \\oplus X \\text{ for all } 1 \\le i \\le k][Ai​=Ai​⊕X&nbsp;for&nbsp;all&nbsp;1≤i≤k]\n(Here, ⊕⊕⊕ denotes bitwise XOR.)\n\nYour goal is to make **all elements of the array pairwise distinct** using the **minimum number of operations**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input:\n\nThe first line contains an integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single integer — the **minimum number of operations** required to make all elements of AAA distinct.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i\\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n0 0\n3\n0 1 2\n4\n0 1 0 1",
        "output": "1\n0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nFor the first test case, one of the possible sequence of operations:\n\nApply ⊕\\oplus⊕ operation to prefix of length k=1k = 1k=1 with X=7X= 7X=7. The new array becomes [7,0][7, 0][7,0] containing all pairwise distinct elements.\n\n\n\nFor the second test case, all elements are already pairwise distinct. So no operations are needed.\n\n\nFor the third test case, one of the possible sequence of operations:\n\nApply ⊕\\oplus⊕ operation to prefix of length k=2k = 2k=2 with X=3X= 3X=3. The new array becomes [3,2,0,1][3, 2, 0, 1][3,2,0,1] containing all pairwise distinct elements."
      }
    ]
  },
